
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ROBIA, please cite this software using its version-specific DOI from Zenodo. Please also cite the associated scientific article listed below."

title: "ROBIA: Rhodamine Object-Based Image Analysis"

authors:
  - family-names: "Peñas-Torramilans"
    given-names: "Raquel"

version: "1.0.0"

abstract: >-
  ROBIA (Rhodamine Object-Based Image Analysis) is an open-source
  workflow developed to detect and map Rhodamine WT (RWT)
  concentrations from UAV-based RGB imagery. It combines RGB
  spectral indices with in situ fluorometric measurements to
  establish site-specific calibration relationships between
  image-derived signals and dye concentrations. The workflow
  includes configurable masking procedures to exclude non-water
  features, such as aquaculture infrastructure, enabling the
  generation of spatially distributed surface tracer concentration
  maps in complex aquatic environments. ROBIA was developed and
  tested in Fangar Bay (NW Mediterranean Sea) and provides a
  reproducible framework for studying tracer dispersion and
  supporting hydrodynamic transport and dispersion modelling.

keywords:
  - Rhodamine WT
  - UAV
  - RGB imagery
  - Object-based image analysis
  - Fluorescent dye tracer
  - Tracer dispersion
  - Coastal environments
  - Aquaculture
  - Surface concentration mapping

